---
/**
 * The on-site quote prompt: a small card in the corner that asks a visitor
 * who has been reading, and typed nothing, for their property address.
 *
 * Ben, 2026-09-23: "we want to ask for quotes for people who just visit the
 * site but don't fill anything out." A visitor who never gives an email
 * cannot be emailed — there is no address, and working one out from their
 * visit would be a CASL/PIPEDA problem — so the only moment to ask is while
 * they are still here. This is the ask.
 *
 * MARKUP ONLY. Base.astro renders it on every page but /contact, /thank-you,
 * /privacy, /terms and /404, and Base.astro's script wires it through
 * scripts/quote-prompt.ts — which holds the rules for WHEN it appears, the
 * longer list of when it never does, and the handoff. The card starts
 * `hidden` and stays that way for half of all browsers: it is an A/B test
 * (lib/experiment.ts, 'quote-prompt'), and the lead count per arm decides
 * whether asking earns quotes or only closes.
 *
 * ONE QUESTION, not two. QuoteFormMini asks for address and email; this
 * card is an interruption and earns only the address. It saves it to the
 * same session draft (lib/quote-draft.ts) and lands on the same prerendered
 * /contact#quote, where the full form asks for the email with the address
 * already filled in — the handoff QuoteFormMini makes, minus a field.
 *
 * NON-MODAL by design: no backdrop, no focus trap, and focus is never moved
 * into it — a visitor mid-sentence in an article should not find their
 * cursor somewhere else. The page stays usable underneath; Escape or the ✕
 * closes it. On phones it sits ABOVE the sticky call bar (MobileCallBar),
 * never over it: during a storm the call is the higher-intent action and
 * nothing may cover it.
 */
---

<div
  id="quote-prompt"
  class="quote-prompt card fixed inset-x-3 z-50 p-5 motion-reduce:transition-none lg:inset-x-auto lg:right-6 lg:w-[360px] lg:p-6"
  role="dialog"
  aria-modal="false"
  aria-labelledby="qp-title"
  aria-describedby="qp-lede"
  hidden
>
  <button
    type="button"
    class="absolute top-3 right-3 inline-flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full text-body transition-colors hover:bg-frost-100 hover:text-ink-950 focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ice-400 focus-visible:outline-none"
    aria-label="Close"
    data-qp-close
  >
    <svg class="h-4 w-4" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
      <path stroke-linecap="round" d="M4 4l8 8M12 4l-8 8" />
    </svg>
  </button>
  {/* Same promise, in the same words, as the hero card: the range is what
      the next screen shows, and "most" because the estimator declines some
      addresses. */}
  <h2 id="qp-title" class="pr-10 font-display text-lg font-bold">Want a price for your property?</h2>
  <p id="qp-lede" class="mt-1.5 text-sm text-body">
    Most addresses get a price range on the next screen. Free, no obligation.
  </p>
  <form class="mt-4 space-y-3" method="get" action="/contact" id="qp-form">
    <div>
      <label class="label" for="qp-address">Property address</label>
      <div class="relative" data-address-autocomplete>
        <input
          class="input"
          id="qp-address"
          name="address"
          type="text"
          required
          minlength="5"
          autocomplete="off"
          role="combobox"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="qp-address-listbox"
          aria-autocomplete="list"
          placeholder="Start typing the address…"
        />
        <ul
          class="address-listbox"
          id="qp-address-listbox"
          role="listbox"
          aria-label="Address suggestions"
          hidden
        ></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <button type="submit" class="btn-primary w-full">Show me my price range</button>
  </form>
  <p class="mt-3 text-center text-[13px] text-body/80">Takes about a minute</p>
</div>

<style>
  /* Above the sticky call bar — MobileCallBar is 68px plus the safe-area
     inset — with a little air. From lg the bar is gone and the card takes
     the corner. */
  .quote-prompt {
    bottom: calc(68px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom) + 0.75rem);
    /* Start state of the slide-up; `.card`'s own transition carries it and
       motion-reduce:transition-none (above) turns it into a plain appear. */
    opacity: 0;
    translate: 0 0.75rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    .quote-prompt {
      bottom: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
  .quote-prompt[data-open] {
    opacity: 1;
    translate: 0 0;
  }
  /* The suggestions open UPWARD here. The card is pinned to the bottom of
     the screen, so a list dropping below the input would run off it — and
     on a phone, under the call bar. */
  .quote-prompt .address-listbox {
    top: auto;
    bottom: 100%;
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 0.375rem;
  }
</style>
